@page "/banking"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components

<h1>Banking & ATMs</h1>
<p>Practical notes for handling money in Thailand (mock info for the MVP).</p>

<div class="card">
    <h3>Major banks</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Bangkok Bank — widest ATM network.</li>
        <li>Kasikornbank (KBank) — good foreign-card support.</li>
        <li>Siam Commercial Bank (SCB) — common in malls.</li>
        <li>Krungthai Bank — often found at airports.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h3>ATM fee notes</h3>
    <p>Foreign cards are typically charged a <strong>220 THB</strong> outward fee per withdrawal, on top of whatever your home bank charges. Withdraw larger amounts less often to cut fees.</p>
    <p>Notify your bank before travel to avoid blocked cards. Visa / Mastercard are accepted at most large merchants; carry some cash for markets and street food.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h3>Currency</h3>
    <p>Thai Baht (THB). Coins: 1, 2, 5, 10 baht. Notes: 20, 50, 100, 500, 1000 baht.</p>
</div>
